# --- CONTRADICTION: Thanks contains Picture(s) ---
:As_ThanksContainsPicture_G2 a dkg:Assertion ;
    rdf:subject :Rel_ThanksContainsPicture_v2 ; rdf:predicate dkg:cardinality ; rdf:object "0..10" ;
    rdfs:comment "Glossary v2: Thanks contains Picture 0..10 (glossary v1: 0..*)" ;
    dkg:source :Art_Glossary_2026_10_v2 ; dkg:confidence dkg:OnArtifact .
:As_ThanksContainsPictures_TH a dkg:Assertion ;
    rdf:subject :Rel_TH_ContainsPictures ; rdf:predicate dkg:cardinality ; rdf:object "1" ;
    rdfs:comment "Thanks model: Thanks contains pictures 1 — mandatory and single, though the label is plural (one value holding a list?)" ;
    dkg:source :Art_Glossary_Thanks ; dkg:confidence dkg:OnArtifact ;
    dkg:contradicts :As_ThanksContainsPicture_G2 .

# --- questions ---
:Q_ThanksRecipients a dkg:Question ;
    skos:prefLabel "Who can a thanks go to — and is it still for a Help?" ;
    rdfs:comment "Glossary: Thanks to Community 0..1, to Grandma Avatar 0..1, for Help 1. Thanks model: recipient 0..* typed Grandma Avatar | Cook | Chef — no Community type, and no reference to a Help at all. A thanks with zero recipients is allowed by the model." ;
    dkg:mentions :Con_Recipient, :Con_Community, :Con_Help, :Rel_ThanksToCommunity, :Rel_ThanksForHelp ;
    dkg:source :Art_Glossary_Thanks, :Art_Glossary_2026_10_v2 ; dkg:locator "recipient branch vs glossary Thanks arrows" ; dkg:confidence dkg:Implied .
:Art_Glossary_Thanks dkg:raises :Q_ThanksRecipients .
:Q_ConsentForMentioning a dkg:Question ;
    skos:prefLabel "Which consent is 'consent for mentioning'?" ;
    rdfs:comment "Thanks model invariant needs a consent for being mentioned; the Consent model (subject, consent Id, consent Text, givenAt, revokedAt) has no purpose or kind — only the consent text could say what is consented to. Sharing would have to ask Consent Management — the context map does draw Consent Management → Sharing, which this invariant would explain; which consent counts is open." ;
    dkg:mentions :R_TH_CookOnlyIfConsentForMentioning, :Con_Consent, :Con_ConsentText, :Ctx_ConsentManagement ;
    dkg:source :Art_Glossary_Thanks ; dkg:locator "purple sticky 'only if consent is given for mentioning'" ; dkg:confidence dkg:Implied .
:Art_Glossary_Thanks dkg:raises :Q_ConsentForMentioning .
:Q_RecipientCookTwice a dkg:Question ;
    skos:prefLabel "What is a recipient of type Cook that contains 0..* Cook?" ;
    rdfs:comment "The model has 'Cook' twice under recipient: as a type value and as a contained 0..* box guarded by consent for mentioning. Mentioned cooks, or the recipient cook(s) themselves?" ;
    dkg:mentions :Con_Cook_RecipientType, :Con_MentionedCook ;
    dkg:source :Art_Glossary_Thanks ; dkg:locator "recipient branch" ; dkg:confidence dkg:Implied .
:Art_Glossary_Thanks dkg:raises :Q_RecipientCookTwice .
:Q_ExampleUUIDsReused rdfs:comment "Thanks model: giver example e1e82a2e-… equals the thanks Id example on the same model; pictures example equals the Recipe model's image URL." ; dkg:source :Art_Glossary_Thanks .
:Q_ChefNotInGlossary rdfs:comment "Thanks model: a Chef recipient is carried as 'Chef name' (0..1, only if type is Chef) — Chefs have no id in any model so far." ; dkg:source :Art_Glossary_Thanks .
:Q_ImagesOrMedia rdfs:comment "Thanks model: 'pictures' with a /media/images/ URL — Pictures, images and media for one thing." ; dkg:source :Art_Glossary_Thanks .

