# sourced to the contract. Existing nodes are NOT re-sourced (no false corroboration).
##############################################################################
:Art_API_MealPlanning_OAS a dkg:Artifact ;
    rdfs:label "Meal Planning API — OpenAPI 3.1, version 1.0.0 (meal-planning.openapi.yaml)" ;
    rdfs:comment "OpenAPI draft from the Meal Planning canvas and Meal Plan model. OAuth2 (meal-plans:read/write), audience external-public. A plan is incomplete (draft) or complete by content — no status or completion command; empty POST allowed; owner immutable, server-assigned; JSON Merge Patch. 'Changed recipient' read as changed meal plan. Diet left as free string: 'no glossary definition'. Records its own x-open-questions." ;
    dkg:mentions :Ctx_MealPlanning ;
    dkg:ingestedAt "2026-10-10"^^xsd:date .
:Q_MealPlanCompleteness a dkg:Question ; skos:prefLabel "Is a meal plan that lacks occasion, servings, meal or courses a valid (incomplete) plan?" ;
    rdfs:comment "The Meal Plan model draws all four with cardinality 1 / 1..10; the canvas allows building step by step. The contract reconciles them as two shapes (draft / complete) without a status." ; dkg:mentions :Con_MealPlan ;
    dkg:source :Art_API_MealPlanning_OAS ; dkg:locator "schemas.MealPlanDraft / MealPlanComplete; x-open-questions" ; dkg:confidence dkg:Inferred .
:Art_API_MealPlanning_OAS dkg:raises :Q_MealPlanCompleteness .
:Q_MealPlanPatchRecipient rdfs:comment "Meal Planning OpenAPI reads 'changed recipient' as 'changed meal plan' (proposal)." ; dkg:source :Art_API_MealPlanning_OAS .
:R_DietMostRestrictive rdfs:comment "Meal Planning OpenAPI: diet vocabulary, ordering and derivation from recipes unresolved; it invents no taxonomy. The Recipe model (ingested after the contract was written) gives vegetarian / vegan / normal." ; dkg:source :Art_API_MealPlanning_OAS .
:Q_IngredientsFromServings rdfs:comment "Meal Planning OpenAPI carries this as an x-open-question and adds no calculation endpoint." ; dkg:source :Art_API_MealPlanning_OAS .
:Q_ExampleUUIDsReused rdfs:comment "Meal Planning OpenAPI: MealPlanLink example uses f64e07f0-… (the cook Id example) as a meal plan id, inheriting the model's reuse." ; dkg:source :Art_API_MealPlanning_OAS .

